{"id":"nova","corpus":"aws","title":"Amazon Nova","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/userguide/what-is-nova.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Amazon Nova"},{"kind":"p","text":"This documentation is for Amazon Nova Version 1. Amazon Nova 2 is now available with new models and enhanced capabilities. New features and documentation updates are published in the Amazon Nova 2 User Guide. For information about what's new in Amazon Nova 2, visit What's new in Amazon Nova 2."},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Nova foundation models deliver frontier intelligence and industry-leading price-performance. Organizations can build and scale generative AI applications with Amazon Nova that are safe, reliable, and cost-effective. Amazon Nova accelerates AI innovation across modalities and use cases - including text, image, video, speech, API calling, and agentic AI. To start building with Amazon Nova, you must access the models through an API using Amazon Bedrock."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Amazon Nova model categories"},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Nova delivers powerful foundation models across three categories: understanding, creative, and speech capabilities."},{"kind":"p","text":"1You can access this model in additional regions through cross-region inference: US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), Europe (Stockholm), Europe (Ireland), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Paris), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Seoul), and Asia Pacific (Mumbai). To learn more, see Improve resilience with cross-region inference."},{"kind":"p","text":"For full model and region support information in Amazon Bedrock, see Supported foundation models in Amazon Bedrock."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Model specifications"},{"kind":"p","text":"The following tables provide detailed specifications for each Amazon Nova model family."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Understanding model specifications"},{"kind":"p","text":"1Optimized for these 15 languages: English, German, Spanish, French, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Arabic, Simplified Chinese, Russian, Hindi, Portuguese, Dutch, Turkish, and Hebrew."},{"kind":"p","text":"2You can access this model in the US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), Europe (Stockholm), Europe (Ireland), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Paris), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Seoul), and Asia Pacific (Mumbai) regions through cross-region inference. Cross-region inference allows you to seamlessly manage unplanned traffic bursts by utilizing compute across different AWS Regions. With cross-region inference, you can distribute traffic across multiple AWS Regions. To learn more about cross-region inference, see Supported Regions and models for inference profiles and Improve resilience with cross-region inference in the Amazon Bedrock User Guide."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Creative and speech model specifications"},{"kind":"p","text":"1By default, the connection limit is 8 minutes, however you can renew the connection and continue the conversation by providing the previous conversation's history."},{"kind":"p","text":"2For a list of supported voices, see Voices available for Amazon Nova Sonic."}],"lemmas":{"amazons":["amazon","amazons"],"nova":["nova","novum"],"documentations":["documentation","documentations"],"versions":["version","versions"],"availables":["availables","available"],"models":["model","models"],"modeling":["modeling","model"],"modeled":["modeled","model"],"enhanced":["enhanced","enhance"],"enhanceds":["enhanceds","enhanced"],"enhances":["enhances","enhance"],"enhancing":["enhancing","enhance"],"capabilities":["capability","capabilities"],"features":["feature","features"],"featuring":["featuring","feature"],"featured":["featured","feature"],"updates":["update","updates"],"updating":["updating","update"],"updated":["updated","update"],"published":["published","publish"],"publisheds":["publisheds","published"],